  "id": "selective-adaptation",
  "term": "selective adaptation",
  "definition": "Selective adaptation is an olfactory processing mechanism in which exposure to odor mixtures changes neural responses in a selective way, with some activity being strengthened and other activity being reduced. In this context, it is used to explain how the brain represents differences and similarities among odors.",
